ed: true, title: "Rejected-candidate reasons repair proposer ranking on arithmetic/modular gates", summary: "logging why the verifier rejected a guess repairs the next-prime proposer at budget 8: the unguided model chooses 7 unsafe rows and causes 172 validation false rejections, while the reason prior reaches 6 accepted rules/216.0 utility and the trained repair reaches 7 accepted rules/245.0 utility with zero false rejections; arithmetic-sequence/modular split sweeps pass, but the delayed-claim stress case has 0 mixed split rows.", explanation: "This is the first feedback loop: rejected verifier rows become reason labels, and those labels improve the next proposal pass. The claim is scoped to the arithmetic-sequence/modular sweeps; delayed_claim remains a stress case. Seed-interval and reason-family artifacts are reported when present so the reporting can distinguish stable proposer repair from a single favorable trace.", source: "results/2026-05-17-substrate-extensions/rejected_candidate_reason_learning.jsonl", chart_kind: "coverage_bar", chart_rows: ((label: "model_score", value: 0.0, false_rejections: 172, unsafe_rules: 7), (label: "reason_prior", value: 216.0, false_rejections: 0, unsafe_rules: 0), (label: "reason_aware", value: 210.0, false_rejections: 0, unsafe_rules: 0), (label: "trained_residual", value: 245.0, false_rejections: 0, unsafe_rules: 0))), (id: "C5.hypothesis_library_promotion", family: "C5", status: "supported", required: true, title: "Certified hypothesis libraries feed back into proposal ranking", summary: "saving repeatedly safe rules helps future tasks: promoted move_to_anchor from 2 tasks/78 covered events with zero false rejections; slot priors raise first-choice certifications from 2 to 4 and budget-8 utility from 0.2119 to 0.5169. Held-out split feedback rows: 30.", explanation: "This makes the hypothesis library a generated claim rather than a roadmap note. Fixture feedback and held-out feedback are separated in machine-readable rows;