 "shared_task_heads 64x32", value: 28.566666666666666, domain: "arc_agi", model_kind: "shared_task_heads", plateau_detected: false), (label: "single_task 64x32", value: 42.8, domain: "arc_agi", model_kind: "single_task", plateau_detected: false), (label: "shared 8x4", value: 39.266666666666666, domain: "arc_agi", model_kind: "shared", plateau_detected: false), (label: "shared_task_heads 8x4", value: 40.5, domain: "arc_agi", model_kind: "shared_task_heads", plateau_detected: false), (label: "single_task 8x4", value: 45.199999999999996, domain: "arc_agi", model_kind: "single_task", plateau_detected: true))), (id: "C8.trace_determinism_audit", family: "C8", status: "supported", required: true, title: "Trace replay semantics are deterministic across float and double runs", summary: "the trace audit checks whether replay meaning survives numeric/runtime changes: 2 traces and 2000 rows, 0 invalid rows, 0 rank-sensitive rows, 0 logged mismatches, same semantic hash: yes.", explanation: "The reproducibility claim is semantic rather than bit-exact: float and double runs may differ in logits and calibration diagnostics, but the replay-semantic trace projection has the same hash and exposes every rank-sensitive row.", source: "results/latest/trace_determinism.jsonl", chart_kind: "coverage_bar", chart_rows: ((label: "float", value: 1000, rank_fp_sensitive_rows: 0, invalid_rows: 0), (label: "double", value: 1000, rank_fp_sensitive_rows: 0, invalid_rows: 0))), (id: "C9.signal_flight_replay_control", family: "C9", status: "supported", required: true, title: "Signal replay-certified WASD ranker improves held-out control utility", summary: "in offline Signal replay, the model ranks recorded WASD choices at top-1 79.76% vs baseline 67.86% (+11.90pp), utility 0.1432 vs 0.1359, regret 0.0073 vs 0.0146, damage 2.38% vs 2.38%, deaths 0.00% vs 0.00%; live shadow frames=74. Closed-loop rollout neural_guarded utility 0.3564 vs baseline -1.4642, reach 12.50% vs 8.33%.", explanation: "This is an application vignette, not a live-control claim: Signal contributes a replay-certified bounded-control surface where the neural component ranks nine WASD candidates and simulator replay owns the outcome labels. The rollout summary is a closed-loop bridge around certified control-target hypotheses, not a multiplayer performance claim.", source: "results/2026-05-17-signal-flight/summary.jsonl", chart_kind: "coverage_bar", chart_rows: ((label: "baseline", value: 67.8571429, regret: 0.014589607), (label: "neural", value: 79.76190480000001, regret: 0.007348488))), (id: "C9.signal_live_neural_active", family: "C9", status: "supported", required: true, title: "Signal guarded neural-active pilot executes live checkpoint-ranked actions", summary: "the live Signal pilot did run checkpoint-ranked neural actions, but only behind guards: 74 recent neural-source rows from checkpoint f12b644ed9fa, p95 inference 0.089 ms, 74 replay-ready rows, protocol-compatible rows=74, safety-gate rows=74, damage events=2, deaths=0; no baseline comparison is claimed.", explanation: "This supports only the existence of guarded live neural-active execution: the running Signal pilot applies checkpoint-ranked WASD actions and logs the fields needed for replay, with a source-header protocol drift guard. It does not yet show that active neural control improves utility or safety versus the heuristic baseline.", source: "results/2026-05-17-signal-flight/live_active_summary.jsonl", chart_kind: "coverage_bar", chart_rows: ((label: "active", value: 74, p95_ms: 0.088958), (label: "replay-ready", value: 74, p95_ms: 0.088958), (label: "protocol-compatible", value: 74, p95_ms: 0.088958), (label: "active frames", value: 74, p95_ms: 0.088958))))

